Team,

A reminder after last month's dispute with the cooperative about a raw milk count.

Before you test any milk or curd sample at the Shirwal chilling plant lab, pour off a portion into a sterile tube, cap it and label it with the lab number. That portion is the retained sample, and it is our only answer if the cooperative or the buyer challenges a result.

Each aliquot is frozen at -18 C and kept for 30 days after the result is reported, then thrown away in the yellow bag unless someone has asked in writing for it to be kept.

The freezer is the small upright one by the window, not the big chest freezer, which holds the plant's own reference cultures.

If the dispute last month had come a week later, we would have had nothing to retest. Please do not skip this step on busy mornings.

Any request to keep a portion longer comes to me, with the reason, and I will write it in the freezer register. Portions for the buyer's own retesting are handed over only against a signed request on the buyer's letterhead, and the handover is written in the same register.

Manisha
